            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "A claim should proceed under \u00a7\u202f1983 only if granting relief would necessarily prevent the state from carrying out the execution."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court affirmed that the claim points toward \u00a7\u202f1983 because the prisoner is not challenging the death sentence itself."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "92b7e67d77f48b236327c2f0a5c6b06d57ba27da70d4277e2f399275ecf9684c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-92b7e67d77f4-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the rule remains true even if the alternative route necessitates a change in state law."
      }
    ],
